  "response_text": " It's normal to feel like an impostor at times, but it's important to remember that everyone has their own unique talents and abilities. Instead of focusing on your perceived shortcomings, try to celebrate your strengths and accomplishments. Surround yourself with supportive colleagues and mentors who can provide guidance and encouragement. Additionally, practice self-compassion and remind yourself that it's okay to make mistakes and learn from them. By shifting your mindset and embracing your own worth, you can overcome the impostor syndrome and thrive in your professional life.\n",
